   202	## Caveats
   203	
   204	- This result is not submission-ready until a funded `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`
   205	  completes the third bare `hard` attempt and the two isolated G9 arms. The
   206	  present bare transcript is partial; the G9 files are authentic but error-only.
   207	- `0/200,000` samples the exact promised prior: ordered, pairwise-distinct
   208	  rationals within the stated bounds. It does not model a learned solver prior
   209	  conditioned on the visibly paired rows. The exact solution count is one, but
   210	  the sampled number alone would not prove that.
   211	- The Track B claim is about unaided execution, not computational
   212	  intractability. A program exploiting the row pairing runs in `O(mn)` scans
   213	  plus 192 arithmetic operations and is faster than generic elimination.
   214	- The adversary panel did not run a commercial LP solver, an SMT solver, a
   215	  lattice-basis attack, or an optical/table parser. The successful exact
   216	  elimination reference covers the zero-level linear system, but those tools
   217	  could reduce wall time or expose other construction signals.
   218	- Some model failure at hard may reflect navigating 40k rendered characters as
   219	  well as discovering the invariant. The answer and exact arithmetic route fit
   220	  G9(c), but prompt navigation remains a confound to be assessed by the three
   221	  oracle arms.
   222	- `canonical_key` uses eight rounds of weighted bipartite color refinement. It
   223	  is invariant under the generated relabellings and strong on this distribution,
   224	  but it is not a complete isomorphism algorithm for arbitrary weighted affine
   225	  systems.
