codex
Implemented a native Track B generator for linear tropical valued CSPs. Section 5.2 explicitly reduces this regime to polynomial-time linear optimization, so a Track A planted-CSP claim would be unjustified. [Paper PDF](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2107.01778)

Deliverables:

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.01778/gen_2107_01778.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.01778/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.01778/README.md)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.01778/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.01778/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.01778/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)
- [External blocker record](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.01778/BLOCKED.md)

All local gates pass. Highlights: 0/200,000 guesses, four attacks at 0/8, Bareiss reference at 8/8 using 1,406,272 operations, and a 192-operation compact route.

The result is not yet submission-ready: the oracle solved `easy` and `medium` 3/3, then failed 0/2 at `hard`; the OpenRouter key reached its total limit before the third attempt. Both G9 auxiliary runs likewise received only HTTP 403 errors. No hardness verdict was fabricated.
